# Template. Copy to  supabase/.env  (which is git-ignored) and edit that copy.
# The Supabase CLI auto-loads supabase/.env and substitutes these values into
# the env(...) refs in config.toml (the [auth.email.smtp] block).
#
# Email in this app is sent by Supabase Auth over SMTP — the confirmation and
# password-reset links. There is no place in the app code that sends email,
# and an API key must never go in the browser bundle, so a provider is wired
# in here as an SMTP relay, not as an SDK call.

# ============================================================================
# DEFAULT: local Mailpit test inbox (http://127.0.0.1:54324)
# Signups work out of the box; mail is captured, never delivered.
# ============================================================================
SMTP_HOST=inbucket
SMTP_PORT=1025
SMTP_USER=mailpit
SMTP_PASS=mailpit
SMTP_ADMIN_EMAIL=arcooreacc@gmail.com

# ============================================================================
# OPTION A — Resend  (https://resend.com)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Free: 3,000 emails/month, 100/day. Best deliverability of the free options.
#
# !!! Without a VERIFIED DOMAIN, Resend only delivers to the address you
#     signed up with (arcooreacc@gmail.com). Every other recipient gets a 403
#     and their signup fails. Fine for testing your own account; NOT usable
#     for real users until you add a domain:
#       Resend dashboard -> Domains -> Add Domain -> add the DNS records it
#       shows -> wait for "Verified" -> set SMTP_ADMIN_EMAIL to an address at
#       that domain (e.g. noreply@yourdomain.com).
#
# Get the key: Resend dashboard -> API Keys -> Create API Key (starts re_).
#
#   SMTP_HOST=smtp.resend.com
#   SMTP_PORT=465
#   SMTP_USER=resend
#   SMTP_PASS=re_your_real_key
#   SMTP_ADMIN_EMAIL=onboarding@resend.dev   # or noreply@yourdomain.com once verified

# ============================================================================
# OPTION B — Brevo  (https://www.brevo.com)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Free: 300/day (9,000/month). Sends to ANY recipient with just a verified
# sender address — no domain needed. Deliverability is a notch below Resend.
#
#   1. Senders, Domains & Dedicated IPs -> Senders -> add arcooreacc@gmail.com,
#      click the link Brevo emails you to verify it.
#   2. SMTP & API -> SMTP tab: copy the "Login", generate an SMTP key.
#
#   SMTP_HOST=smtp-relay.brevo.com
#   SMTP_PORT=587
#   SMTP_USER=<the Login from step 2>
#   SMTP_PASS=<the xsmtpsib-... key from step 2>
#   SMTP_ADMIN_EMAIL=arcooreacc@gmail.com

# After editing supabase/.env:
#   ./.tools/supabase.exe stop && ./.tools/supabase.exe start
# To carry it to the hosted project (part of a full deploy):
#   ./.tools/supabase.exe config push

# --- Cloudflare Turnstile (bot protection on login + signup) --------------
# Free at https://dash.cloudflare.com -> Turnstile. Put the Site Key in
# public/js/env.js (not secret - it ships in the page); put the Secret Key
# here, then set [auth.captcha] enabled = true in supabase/config.toml.
TURNSTILE_SECRET=

# ============================================================================
# Social sign-in - Google / Microsoft / Apple
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Buttons already exist in the app (hidden). To turn a provider on: register
# an OAuth app with it, put its client id + secret below, set enabled = true
# in [auth.external.<provider>] in config.toml, add the provider name
# ('google' / 'azure' / 'apple') to window.SITESTOCK_OAUTH_PROVIDERS in
# public/js/env.js, then restart (or `config push` for hosted).
#
# The redirect / callback URL every provider must be told to allow is
# Supabase's own:  https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
# (locally: http://127.0.0.1:54321/auth/v1/callback). NOT the app's URL.
#
# GOOGLE  (free; needs a Google account, ~20 min)
#   1. https://console.cloud.google.com -> create a project.
#   2. APIs & Services -> OAuth consent screen -> External -> fill app name,
#      support email, the privacy-policy + terms URLs, your domain. Publish
#      it or leave "Testing" (max 100 users, fine for a beta).
#   3. Credentials -> Create credentials -> OAuth client ID -> Web application.
#      Authorised redirect URI = the Supabase callback URL above.
#   4. Copy the Client ID and Client secret into the two vars below.
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_SECRET=
#
# MICROSOFT / AZURE  (free; needs a Microsoft/Azure account)
#   1. https://portal.azure.com -> Microsoft Entra ID -> App registrations ->
#      New registration. Redirect URI (type "Web") = the Supabase callback URL.
#   2. Copy the "Application (client) ID" -> AZURE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID.
#   3. Certificates & secrets -> New client secret -> copy its VALUE (not the
#      id) -> AZURE_OAUTH_SECRET. It expires; note the date.
#   4. Leave [auth.external.azure] url unset for "any Microsoft account", or
#      set it to a single tenant's authority to restrict to one organisation.
AZURE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
AZURE_OAUTH_SECRET=
#
# APPLE  (needs the Apple Developer Program, $99/year, an adult - see the
#         launch checklist; this is the heaviest of the three)
#   1. developer.apple.com -> Certificates, Identifiers & Profiles.
#   2. Identifiers -> add an App ID with "Sign In with Apple" enabled, then a
#      Services ID -> that Services ID string is APPLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID.
#      Configure it with your domain and the Supabase callback URL as the
#      Return URL.
#   3. Keys -> add a key with "Sign In with Apple" -> download the .p8.
#   4. From the .p8 + your Team ID + Key ID + Services ID, generate the
#      client-secret JWT (Apple's docs, or a small script). That JWT is
#      APPLE_OAUTH_SECRET. It has a max lifetime of 6 months - set a reminder
#      to regenerate it.
APPLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
APPLE_OAUTH_SECRET=
